## Session 1 summary (ccloop 46efd8b6)

**Criteria NOT yet met** — substantial progress: 4 root causes found and fixed (RULE-4 instrumented chains), 2 previously-impossible cells went green, 1 new regression diagnosed with mitigation built but untested.

**Root causes proven + fixed this session** (all param-gated, default-on, uncommitted in tree):
1. **Stale-HB evict-ring replay** (`evict_ring_monotonic`): plain cacheable heartbeat reads made peer `head_seq` jump backward → up to 28 already-consumed DIR_MODIFY entries replayed → ~6 spurious dir-invalidation events/sec during pure reads. This was the engine behind the whole "32-node coherency variance" family.
2. **iread-EX starvation** (`iread_pr`): extent-map loads escalated to cluster EX; 12/32 nodes starved 3×120s → `rc=-110` → FS shutdowns during read-only verify. Now cluster PR + local EXCL (GFS2 model).
3. **Per-miss O(dir) datascan** (`dscan_gen_gate`): 459 disk IOs / 112ms per negative lookup; now one scan per coherency-state change. → **cache_coherency@32 PASS 32/32** (build DDB9E83B, first ever).
4. **One-op-per-tenure dir-EX rotation** (`dir_ex_tenure_floor`): mid-op BASTs honored at op end = 1 create per cluster rotation. Floor → **crash_consistency@32 PASS 32/32** (build 0BD98E9E) — but the 300ms window piled 31 waiters per tenure and tripped a **pre-existing orphan-live release-abort loop** ending in a **stranded on-disk EX** (slot gm=5, no in-core holder) that regressed cache_coherency+dlm_scaling to 0/32.

**Current build 30E6BF7F** (built, not yet tested): floor converted to a sliding 25ms batch-grace — batches back-to-back writers while bounding waiter pile-up.

**Next session**: (1) run the trio (cache_coherency, crash_consistency, dlm_scaling) @32 on 30E6BF7F; (2) if the strand recurs, root-fix the orphan-abort path (force-clear own slot bit, sess15 FIX-H2 strike escalation); (3) dir_reuse@16/@32 (budgets 2240s/4480s); (4) full-ladder re-sweep on the final build at every node count; (5) only then write the criteria marker. Full state + recipes in ccmemory `AAA-ccloop46ef-sess1-FOUR-FIXES-scoreboard`.

